// Doom's view of a level in ent-lang (examples/doom: data.ent,
// render.ent, things.ent, sprites.ent): the textures put together, the
// walk through the level's tree, the walls, floors, ceilings and sky
// drawn, and the level's things by their sprites. E1M1 of the
// shareware WAD from 92 places (Inputs/doom/views.ent), all the pictures
// as one number: that of pictures that are the reference's pixel for
// pixel, but for four pixels the original reads from past a lump's end
// (examples/doom/check/view.sh compares them). Runs where the WAD
// is (examples/doom/reference/fetch.sh fetches it).
// REQUIRES: doom-wad
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cp %doom-wad %t/doom1.wad
// RUN: cd %t && %ent run -I %S/../../examples/doom -I %S/Inputs/doom \
// RUN:     %S/../../examples/doom/check/frames_check.ent | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:     pictures 92: 1017864855
// CHECK-NOT: {{.}}
